tor_primary":5.0,"sector_secondary":29.41,"sector_tertiary":65.58},{"period":"2025Q4","area":"Rural","emp_ratio":43.87,"participation":49.28,"pop_share":46.0,"su1":10.98,"su2":16.63,"su3":25.77,"su4":30.49,"wap_share":50.82,"precarious":34.92,"sector_primary":50.7,"sector_secondary":18.6,"sector_tertiary":30.7},{"period":"2025Q4","area":"Urban","emp_ratio":43.15,"participation":50.52,"pop_share":54.0,"su1":14.58,"su2":19.37,"su3":30.56,"su4":34.45,"wap_share":61.67,"precarious":10.96,"sector_primary":5.8,"sector_secondary":27.9,"sector_tertiary":66.3},{"period":"2026Q2","area":"Rural","emp_ratio":43.44,"participation":48.58,"pop_share":46.0,"su1":10.57,"su2":13.32,"su3":29.98,"su4":32.14,"wap_share":50.1,"precarious":40.37,"sector_primary":54.28,"sector_secondary":18.63,"sector_tertiary":27.09},{"period":"2026Q2","area":"Urban","emp_ratio":40.38,"participation":47.57,"pop_share":54.0,"su1":15.12,"su2":19.27,"su3":32.38,"su4":35.69,"wap_share":62.56,"precarious":17.09,"sector_primary":9.3,"sector_secondary":25.48,"sector_tertiary":65.22}],"electricity":{"years":[2004,2008,2014,2023],"rows":[{"wilaya":"Hodh Ech Chargi","values":[1.3,4.8,9.8,17.0]},{"wilaya":"Hodh El Gharbi","values":[1.5,7.8,12.3,19.6]},{"wilaya":"Assaba","values":[8.7,9.3,17.0,24.0]},{"wilaya":"Gorgol","values":[5.3,7.7,11.2,21.4]},{"wilaya":"Brakna","values":[6.5,8.6,11.7,32.6]},{"wilaya":"Trarza","values":[8.4,7.0,23.4,45.5]},{"wilaya":"Adrar","values":[28.3,33.4,52.0,66.2]},{"wilaya":"Dakhlet Nouadhibou","values":[65.5,92.2,91.4,96.0]},{"wilaya":"Tagant","values":[6.0,14.2,14.2,26.8]},{"wilaya":"Guidimakha","values":[2.0,3.6,9.9,13.2]},{"wilaya":"Tiris Zemmour","values":[89.4,91.0,92.9,92.0]},{"wilaya":"Inchiri","values":[46.3,54.5,69.3,73.3]},{"wilaya":"Nouakchott","values":[62.6,75.9,84.1,90.5]},{"wilaya":"Mauritania","values":[20.4,30.7,38.6,48.7]}]},"literature":[{"title":"Urbanisation without industrialisation","text":"Resource exporters urbanise without industrialising: rents are spent in towns on trade and services ('consumption cities'), while manufacturing stays small (Gollin, Jedwab & Vollrath 2016). Mauritania — iron ore, gold, fish — fits the pattern."},{"title":"Cities that grow faster than their networks","text":"African cities urbanise at lower incomes than other regions, so investment in housing, roads and utilities lags behind people: they are 'crowded, disconnected and costly' (Lall, Henderson & Venables 2017)."},{"title":"Drought pushes people to towns","text":"Drier conditions speed up rural–urban migration in sub-Saharan Africa (Barrios, Bertinelli & Strobl 2006; Henderson, Storeygard & Deichmann 2017). The droughts of the 1970s–80s turned a nomadic country (78% nomads in the mid-1960s) into a settled one."},{"title":"Electricity in fast-growing cities","text":"Over 100 million urban Africans live under the grid without a connection, and reliability falls as cities spread (Odarno 2019). In Nouakchott — more than half of national demand — demand grows about 7% a year and long outages returned in 2025."},{"title":"Other strains","text":"Flooding: the flooded share of Nouakchott rose from 0.07% (1994) to 3.96% (2024) as groundwater rises and soils are sealed (Aillal et al. 2026). Housing: about a third of households lived in precarious dwellings (2014 population policy). Water, sanitation, transport over a low-density city, and urban jobs all have to keep up."}],"sources":["ANSADE, Annuaire des statistiques sociodémographiques 2025 (tables 1.1, 1.2, 6.1).","RGPH 1988, 2000, 2013 and 2023 (communes), as compiled in Wikipedia, List of cities in Mauritania.","République Islamique de Mauritanie (2014). Déclaration nationale de politique de population.","World Bank WDI: SP.URB.TOTL.IN.ZS (urban population, % of total; UN World Urbanization Prospects).","Gollin, D., Jedwab, R., Vollrath, D. (2016). Urbanization with and without industrialization. Journal of Economic Growth 21(1).","Lall, S. V., Henderson, J. V., Venables, A. J. (2017). Africa's Cities: Opening Doors to the World. World Bank.","Barrios, S., Bertinelli, L., Strobl, E. (2006). Climatic change and rural–urban migration: the case of sub-Saharan Africa. Journal of Urban Economics 60(3).","Henderson, J. V., Storeygard, A., Deichmann, U. (2017). Has climate change driven urbanization in Africa? Journal of Development Economics 124.","Odarno, L. (2019). Closing Sub-Saharan Africa's electricity access gap: why cities must be part of the solution. World Resources Institute.","Aillal, M. M. et al. (2026). Multi-temporal analysis of Nouakchott floods (1994–2024). Journal of Water and Land Development 69."]}